id: pm-slack-kaku
title: Drop inert pm manifest key and guard the closed manifest vocabulary
description: "pm-cli treats the extension manifest vocabulary as a closed set of keys; since pm-cli 2026.8.19 any other top-level manifest.json key yields a manifest_unknown_key warning. This repo's manifest.json carried an inert top-level pm key ({\"compatibility\":\"v2\"}) that nothing in src/, scripts/, or test/ ever read. It caused strict-assertion failures downstream (unbraind/pm-linear PRs #75/#76 expect findings codes exactly ['pm_min_version_unmet'] but got ['manifest_unknown_key','pm_min_version_unmet']). This change deletes only that key, bumps the dev-dependency pin of @unbrained/pm-cli from 2026.8.15 to 2026.8.22 so the regression test can detect unknown manifest keys (the older CLI predates the detection), and adds test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts asserting zero manifest_unknown_key findings. The changelog scripts already carried unbounded-read --pm-arg flags, so no script changes were needed."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T17:50:42.152Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T18:59:47.729Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T17:53:08.237Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T17:53:08.237Z"
claim_principal: ox-alpha
author: ox-alpha
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T17:50:55.072Z",ox-alpha,"Regression verification: re-adding the pm key programmatically made test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts fail with a manifest_unknown_key finding (path: pm, required: pm, current: 2026.8.22); after restoring the manifest the test passes again (1 pass / 0 fail). npm test: 80 tests, 80 pass, 0 fail (exit 0). npm run release:check: exit 0 (typecheck, build, docstring gate, coverage gate, audit:prod, pack dry-run, changelog:check all green; changelog scripts already had unbounded-read --pm-arg flags). Pinned ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit: exit 0, ok:true, 3 advisory provenance warnings only."
files[4]{path,scope}:
  manifest.json,project
  package-lock.json,project
  package.json,project
  test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,path,scope,note}:
  "PM_PATH=\"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/pm-mv-pm-slack\" PM_GLOBAL_PATH=\"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/pm-mv-g-pm-slack\" node --test test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts",test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts,project,"Runs the manifest-vocabulary guard against isolated tracker roots so it cannot touch the real workspace. Uses ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} rather than a hardcoded /tmp: the recorded command should be runnable by whoever reads it, including on a machine where TMPDIR is set elsewhere, and a concrete scratch path pins the record to one environment."
close_reason: "Closed: inert top-level pm manifest key removed from manifest.json after grep-verified confirmation that nothing in index.ts, scripts/, or test/ reads it; @unbrained/pm-cli dev pin bumped 2026.8.15 -> 2026.8.22 so unknown manifest keys are detectable; added test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts asserting zero manifest_unknown_key findings — verified it fails when the pm key is re-added and passes once removed (pm test linked run passed, tests_count=1). Gates: npm test 80/80 pass exit 0; npm run release:check exit 0 (changelog scripts already had unbounded --pm-arg flags); pinned ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit exit 0."
body: ""
